pkgcheck_request(3)

# NAME

pkgcheck_request - seal one exact native package check request

# SYNOPSIS

```
auto request = pkgcheck::check_request::seal(
    transaction, check_node_identity, successful_build_result);
```

# DESCRIPTION

A request is valid only when the named node is a transaction check action with a
unique *build_before_check* predecessor. Both nodes must retain the same resolver
selection. The successful build result must match the selected package release,
source snapshot, architectures, and exact source-owned check program.

The request retains the complete build result and a projection of package inputs
whose scope is exactly *check*.

# ERRORS

Admission throws *pkgcheck::error* for wrong actions, absent or inconsistent
phase authority, failed builds, and mismatched build authority.

# SEE ALSO

*libpkgcheck*(3), *pkgcheck_result*(3)
